  "intro": [
    "Flexibars are formed from multiple layers of thin copper strips, insulated with a high resistance, self-extinguishing PVC compound. Holes are punched directly through the laminates and connected, so lugs are not needed. That cuts labour and process cost and makes installation easier.",
    "They replace large cables with lugs and solid rigid busbars in a panel, need less space for a given current, and bend and twist easily."
  ],
  "features": [
    "Copper lamination with durable polymer insulation",
    "Internal laminates are insulated to allow bending and twisting",
    "Terminals are made by punching directly through the copper lamination",
    "Removes the cost of lugs and reduces labour cost",
    "Alternative to large cables with lugs and to solid rigid busbars",
    "Needs less space for high current; cross section about 40% lower than a cable",
    "Aesthetically improves the panel and reduces the number of connections",
    "Guaranteed insulation thickness, including at the corner",
    "Available to your drawing"
  ],
